DevilutionX for Debian (Walnut / PS3)
=====================================

Licence: NOT free software
--------------------------
DevilutionX is under the Sustainable Use License 1.0 (the full text is in
/usr/share/doc/devilutionx/copyright). It allows use, copying and
modification for your own internal business purposes or for non-commercial
or personal use, and distribution only free of charge and for
non-commercial purposes. That is not an OSI or DFSG free licence, so this
package is non-free in Debian's terms. It is built and distributed here
free of charge, for non-commercial use only. Do not sell it, bundle it in a
product, or offer it for money.

The package's Section stays "games" on purpose: in this repository a
Section of non-free/* or local/* marks licensed game data that is never
public, and this package is the engine only.

This is a modified version
--------------------------
This package is NOT the unmodified upstream DevilutionX 1.5.5. It carries
patches of ours (see the source package):

  0001  sound: open the audio device in the host byte order
        (AUDIO_S16SYS), so the engine plays on big-endian machines.

It is also built without ZeroTier (online) multiplayer and without Discord
integration. Problems with this build are not upstream's: report them to
the packager, not to the DevilutionX project.

Game data
---------
No game data is part of this package. Diablo's DIABDAT.MPQ (and Hellfire's
hf*.mpq) belong to Blizzard and come from your own copy of the game; the
free shareware version's spawn.mpq also works. Put the files in
~/.local/share/diasurgical/devilution/ (or /usr/share/diasurgical/devilution/).
